From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:31:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): notify completed, failed and conflicting
 synchronization

Motivation: a person who closed the window learns about a failure or a
conflict only by opening DriveSync again; nothing on the desktop says that a
run finished, failed or needs a decision.

Changes: each account's status is followed on transitions only: a run that
dispatched at least one operation and returns to idle posts "Google Drive is
up to date"; a non-retryable failure, a worker that could not start, a
conflict or a folder that needs a decision each post one notification with
Open DriveSync. An event is told only once its phase has lasted two
seconds, and a failure, conflict or decision only once until the account is
idle again: the engine retries a blocked item, and each retry passes through
other phases. Notifications are replaced per account and kind, and a later
completed run withdraws the account's earlier failure and conflict
notifications. The item that needs attention stays listed in the window, as
before; nothing is retried, resolved or overwritten by a notification.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy -D warnings, unit tests for the
transitions (one completion per run with changes, none for an idle check,
failures and conflicts on entry only); in a Plasma 6.7 session against a
local stand-in of Google's endpoints each of completion, conflict and failure
reached Plasma's notification server once, with DriveSync's desktop entry;
the build without this change posts none.

Limitations: the stand-in's 403 storageQuotaExceeded reaches the person as
"an item could not be synchronized": the engine treats an unlisted Google
error during a mutation as an uncertain effect, so the quota reason itself
is not carried to the status.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (branch order299 of the edition's DriveSync fork)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
